# Paths exempt from stampscan (gitignore-style globs, one per line).
# Keep this list SHORT and reasoned — every entry is a hole in the boundary.
#
# Note what this file does NOT do: an ignored path is exempt from being
# scanned FOR stamped blocks. It is still perfectly usable as a canonical
# `source=` target — a file can be a source without ever being a stamp.

# Review briefs and verdicts: frozen once landed, and they quote probe
# material RAW by nature — a pass that reproduces a marker failure mode has to
# write the marker down to show it. Five config errors came from this store
# alone before the parser learned about code context, and one brief added
# another minutes after being written (2026-07-26 cold pass ST1, counsel).
#
# Measured honestly, 2026-08-06: the parser fix ALONE now clears the whole
# live tree — every marker in this store today sits in a fence or a code
# span, so this entry gates nothing at present. It is kept as the standing net
# for the named residual (a raw line-start marker in bare prose), because this
# is precisely the store where that shape is written on purpose, and because
# these files are frozen — a future brief cannot be re-edited to comply.
docs/reviews/

# Harness-native worktrees nest INSIDE the repo (.gitignore), so a scan rooted
# at the repo top re-reads a whole second copy of the tree — another session's
# in-flight state, whose stamped blocks may be mid-edit by design. The house
# net every sibling ignore file already carries.
.claude/worktrees/
